WEBVTT

00:00:45.790 --> 00:00:50.615
Here is the same purple pen in the expert demonstration and the
current episode.

00:00:50.615 --> 00:00:54.940
MXI projects the grasp center into both wrist views.

00:00:54.940 --> 00:00:57.077
Now watch the left hand approach.

00:00:57.077 --> 00:00:59.302
The pen moves toward the cross.

00:00:59.302 --> 00:01:02.902
The fingers close, and the pen rises with the hand.

00:01:02.902 --> 00:01:08.502
A shared geometric reference helps the policy relate its own grasp to
the demonstration.

00:01:09.270 --> 00:01:10.982
One image gives a direction.

00:01:10.982 --> 00:01:13.832
The distance is still open along that ray.

00:01:13.832 --> 00:01:16.920
Now select the same rim point in the wrist view.

00:01:16.920 --> 00:01:19.845
A second ray narrows down the location.

00:01:19.845 --> 00:01:24.732
With both camera poses, MXI estimates a position from the two images.

00:01:24.732 --> 00:01:29.882
In this recorded example, the head-camera depth is about fifty-three
centimetres.

00:01:29.882 --> 00:01:34.245
The estimate returns to the agent as context for its next action.

00:02:06.820 --> 00:02:10.798
On 22 tasks shared with the original report,

00:02:10.798 --> 00:02:15.590
the category-balanced score rose from 52.27 to 80.58.
